Job Title: Watershed Enhancement Team Leader

Work Term: 4-month (May 1 - August 29, 2025) and 7-month (May 1 - November 28, 2025) interim positions available.

Hours: 40 hours/week during the summer and 37.5 hours/week in the fall, Monday to Friday with some weekend and evening shifts.

About the Employer

Dillon Consulting Limited (www.dillon.ca) is a well-established, employee-owned professional consulting firm operating across Canada and internationally. We offer a wide range of consulting and design services related to facilities, the environment, community development and infrastructure.

Job Summary

Dillon is currently seeking qualified candidates for the interim position of Watershed Enhancement Team Leader to assist in the delivery of the 2025 City of Surrey Salmon Habitat Restoration Program (SHaRP), which will be celebrating 30 years of successful watershed enhancement and environmental stewardship. The Watershed Enhancement Team Leaders will lead a team of high school students operating from the SHaRP office located in Surrey, BC to implement watershed restoration prescriptions under the direction of the SHaRP Program Coordinator and Client. This is a field-based position with a focus on invasive plant removal and riparian restoration. Successful applicants will receive experience and training in environmental restoration and watershed enhancement techniques.

Responsibilities
• Collaboration with other post-secondary students to implement environmental initiatives that will enhance streams and riparian areas within the City of Surrey;

• Training and supervision of field and outreach crews consisting of up to 10 secondary school students;

• Completion of field activities such as invasive plant removal, fish habitat assessments, stream bank erosion protection and stabilization, native plant installation, and water quality sampling;

• Environment-focused education and public outreach to City residents and businesses;

• Planning, implementation and supervision of daily activities;

• Regular tracking of project deliverables and providing progress updates to supervisors; and

• Contribution of a final report to the Client.

While Dillon would like to thank all applicants, only candidates considered for an interview will be contacted. For more information on the SHaRP program, please visit www.surrey.ca/SHaRP or watch our SHaRP video playlist on the City of Surrey YouTube channel.

